                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "5368190c-85bc-4c5f-b254-bd6089a5d07a",
                        "entry_id": "cc790736-69ac-3e77-b30e-1222bdac30d0",
                        "tags": [
                            "masculine"
                        ],
                        "form": "patient"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "099b4352-7601-3bba-a196-0c402cdeaf3c",
                        "entry_id": "cc790736-69ac-3e77-b30e-1222bdac30d0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Celle sur qui on agit, par opposition à agent, celui qui agit."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "29de7b8f-f972-3008-a657-c2529f337ac5",
                        "entry_id": "cc790736-69ac-3e77-b30e-1222bdac30d0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Celle qui est entre les mains des chirurgiens ou des médecins, et plus généralement, d’un personnel soignant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d08eea1f-fac9-417b-b190-1a3aa5b4310c",
                                "sense_id": "29de7b8f-f972-3008-a657-c2529f337ac5",
                                "text": "Si une patiente souffrant de thyroïdite d’Hashimoto veut malgré tout se voir prescrire une contraception par hormones de synthèse, il faut suivre attentivement sa fonction thyroïdienne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e320b498-5d41-4dbd-88d8-90e2ff885d61",
                                "sense_id": "29de7b8f-f972-3008-a657-c2529f337ac5",
                                "text": "Qu’une solution soit meilleure pour les médecins ne signifie pas qu’elle soit meilleure pour la patiente."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c75c30aa-c0b4-4d2f-8cac-98f048f04cb1",
                        "source_entry_id": "cc790736-69ac-3e77-b30e-1222bdac30d0",
                        "target_lang_word": "Patientin",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Patientin",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c01ac7b8-aa4f-3674-a56a-8d7fb09b4efc",
                                        "entry_id": "803a86ba-2df7-359d-9974-93fc311fe22b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "weibliche Person, die sich in medizinischer Behandlung befindet"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74f29f5d-20d0-4ac4-92e1-0d419f3447d5",
                                                "sense_id": "c01ac7b8-aa4f-3674-a56a-8d7fb09b4efc",
                                                "text": "„Auf dem Stundenplan der Patientin standen Einzel- und Gruppengespräche, Physiotherapie, Massagen, Sporttherapie, Entspannungsübungen und Ernährungsberatung.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9313abe4-88f6-4dc5-8698-e8c655432222",
                                                "sense_id": "c01ac7b8-aa4f-3674-a56a-8d7fb09b4efc",
                                                "text": "„Uns wurde also das Recht zugebilligt, Patientinnen aufzunehmen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c252012e-14e7-4bda-a335-1703c27a8b44",
                                                "sense_id": "c01ac7b8-aa4f-3674-a56a-8d7fb09b4efc",
                                                "text": "„Die Patientin schien eher ein Herzproblem zu haben.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1b2a25e3-3b2a-4e0b-80b0-22d67be0f810",
                                                "sense_id": "c01ac7b8-aa4f-3674-a56a-8d7fb09b4efc",
                                                "text": "„An den Mundschleimhäuten bilden sich Geschwüre, so daß die Patientin allenfalls trinken, aber nichts essen kann.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4816781e-fa3b-4735-a80f-e5d9d538f42c",
                                                "sense_id": "c01ac7b8-aa4f-3674-a56a-8d7fb09b4efc",
                                                "text": "„Die beiden Patientinnen waren anscheinend so beeindruckt von der Medizinersprache, dass sie versuchten, dieses Sprachgebaren zu imitieren.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c693e650-97df-46d9-8642-fcc810226514",
                        "source_entry_id": "cc790736-69ac-3e77-b30e-1222bdac30d0",
                        "target_lang_word": "patient",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "patient",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8017ccd9-3832-3013-8060-86f16c956f54",
                                        "entry_id": "36e92612-bed2-3ea4-98c3-55ab8a57ad83",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Willing to wait if necessary; not losing one's temper while waiting."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "of a person"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe4e996d-6b21-4a42-a68e-695cabdc2aa5",
                                                "sense_id": "8017ccd9-3832-3013-8060-86f16c956f54",
                                                "text": "Be patient: your friends will arrive in a few hours."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b702db84-5b85-43af-b404-247d0a8c0527",
                                                "sense_id": "8017ccd9-3832-3013-8060-86f16c956f54",
                                                "text": "Asari Cultural VI: Due to our lifespan-sometimes reaching 1,000 years of age-we are patient in our decisions, and prefer long-term solutions over short-term gains."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "be90a50d-8aa3-31cb-9085-f8814c230dac",
                                        "entry_id": "36e92612-bed2-3ea4-98c3-55ab8a57ad83",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Constant in pursuit or exertion; persevering; calmly diligent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72105cf8-495a-4868-87b5-b44d9df21247",
                                                "sense_id": "be90a50d-8aa3-31cb-9085-f8814c230dac",
                                                "text": "a patient wait"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8fda5af5-2d71-4ba0-9de6-86c924aa46d0",
                                                "sense_id": "be90a50d-8aa3-31cb-9085-f8814c230dac",
                                                "text": "patient analysis"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0fc464ff-5af5-40f5-ae8e-93efae877dc0",
                                                "sense_id": "be90a50d-8aa3-31cb-9085-f8814c230dac",
                                                "text": "c. 1692, Sir Isaac Newton, letter to Dr. Richard Bentley\nWhatever I have done […] is due to […] patient thought."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e67b41aa-bb44-4993-b4ae-7cc4ce91406f",
                                                "sense_id": "be90a50d-8aa3-31cb-9085-f8814c230dac",
                                                "text": "patient endeavour"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95ceb107-8f77-4591-8f14-8ada86918bfb",
                                                "sense_id": "be90a50d-8aa3-31cb-9085-f8814c230dac",
                                                "text": "December 15, 2016, Hettie Judah in the New York Times, Beloved Children’s-Book Characters, in Their Own Immersive World\n“Her personal life and her art were very intertwined: You can’t really separate them,” explains Sophia Jansson. “She mirrored her own a reality onto a fictional reality.” And this is perhaps the nub of the Moomin’s enduring appeal: a combination of adventuresome spirit and philosophy, all of which Jansson derived from close and patient observation, of human relationships and of the natural world alike."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "191d1790-539e-45ef-bdb7-a512f7c65346",
                                                "sense_id": "be90a50d-8aa3-31cb-9085-f8814c230dac",
                                                "text": "In contrast, the Westminster Gazette in 1912 was much more positive about railway staff, praising the \"...army of porters hustling and bustling hither and thither with barrows groaning under the weight of bags and baggage and... the ever-patient and long-suffering guards, courteously giving information and advice to the querulous passengers... to the porter the Christmas season means a continuous round of heavy labour, extremely tiring to both nerves and temper, and this fact the public too often seem either to forget or ignore.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae76a8f0-92c6-3520-a9a5-383304304fcd",
                                        "entry_id": "36e92612-bed2-3ea4-98c3-55ab8a57ad83",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Physically able to suffer or bear."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "077cc484-8528-4a50-a6d8-9a7123a79793",
                                                "sense_id": "ae76a8f0-92c6-3520-a9a5-383304304fcd",
                                                "text": "To this outward structure was joined that strength of constitution, patient of severest toil and hardship; insomuch that for the most part of his life, in the fiercest extremity of cold, he took no other advantage of a fire, than at the greatest distance that he could, to look upon it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "patient",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b2bcecc9-00db-325a-846e-d6e3529f88f1",
                                        "entry_id": "9d9096a5-f203-33c2-a1b6-faf2ae7b48c1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person or animal that receives health care from a doctor, nurse, dentist, allied health practitioner, or other person educated in health care."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "048a2896-de24-4c11-b2fd-76cddc03dc0b",
                                                "sense_id": "b2bcecc9-00db-325a-846e-d6e3529f88f1",
                                                "text": "Hello, is your practice currently accepting new patients? I'd like to become a patient there if so."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1485258-487e-496b-91ce-bc1bbcbc3cf9",
                                                "sense_id": "b2bcecc9-00db-325a-846e-d6e3529f88f1",
                                                "text": "At the veterinary clinic, caring for the patients successfully and dealing with the patients’ owners successfully are both necessary skills."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15ed7e30-dd13-4b2b-aec1-1d29bf950b9b",
                                                "sense_id": "b2bcecc9-00db-325a-846e-d6e3529f88f1",
                                                "text": "The slightest effort made the patient cough. He would stand leaning on a stick and holding a hand to his side, and when the paroxysm had passed it left him shaking."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50f6386f-5ea2-4d72-bc33-02cbf770c85f",
                                                "sense_id": "b2bcecc9-00db-325a-846e-d6e3529f88f1",
                                                "text": "An artificial kidney these days still means a refrigerator-sized dialysis machine. Such devices mimic[…]real kidneys[…]. But they are nothing like as efficient, and can cause bleeding, clotting and infection—not to mention inconvenience for patients, who typically need to be hooked up to one three times a week for hours at a time."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "34a48b1a-222f-37a7-beab-532f2ab64a8b",
                                        "entry_id": "9d9096a5-f203-33c2-a1b6-faf2ae7b48c1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The noun or noun phrase that is semantically on the receiving end of a verb's action."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2b2a992-2ecf-4fdb-b70d-63b2293257a8",
                                                "sense_id": "34a48b1a-222f-37a7-beab-532f2ab64a8b",
                                                "text": "The subject of a passive verb is usually a patient."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e48d9331-e9b6-4b95-babf-d5c1a31a441c",
                                                "sense_id": "34a48b1a-222f-37a7-beab-532f2ab64a8b",
                                                "text": "The number of a first or second person participant is generally marked for both agent and patient in all aspects."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "43303e74-8af4-40dd-8fc5-1bc233beef9d",
                                                "sense_id": "34a48b1a-222f-37a7-beab-532f2ab64a8b",
                                                "text": "Since we have argued that the absolutive argument in Dyirbal is the grammatical subject of its clause, we must conclude that in the antipassive construction the agent replaces the patient as grammatical subject."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "628998af-71eb-3afa-afad-26154bd913d9",
                                        "entry_id": "9d9096a5-f203-33c2-a1b6-faf2ae7b48c1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who, or that which, is passively affected; a passive recipient."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf2eb7ea-1cf8-4f5c-9824-1c210007945a",
                                                "sense_id": "628998af-71eb-3afa-afad-26154bd913d9",
                                                "text": "Malice is a passion so impetuous and precipitate, that it often involves the agent and the patient."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca32dbbf-0f95-47db-8937-e8bcee9f90da",
                                                "sense_id": "628998af-71eb-3afa-afad-26154bd913d9",
                                                "text": "For it seems clear that the subject of change is the changed, i.e. the patient -- on one proviso. the proviso is that there be an agent or changer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d910f290-7dcf-4a21-afc6-a92166d57f64",
                                                "sense_id": "628998af-71eb-3afa-afad-26154bd913d9",
                                                "text": "How does a person change from a patient to an agent in shaping and living a course of life?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "914f2b08-c38e-44a2-a407-841c9603b1ca",
                                                "sense_id": "628998af-71eb-3afa-afad-26154bd913d9",
                                                "text": "According to the tradition, when an agent acts on a patient, the change is located in the patient. If the patient reacts on the agent, then the agent is a patient in the new relation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5417dbea-fb97-4c76-a8c9-da4e0f6c8af2",
                                                "sense_id": "628998af-71eb-3afa-afad-26154bd913d9",
                                                "text": "The starting point is that all events involve an agent and a patient. Agents and patients are modelled as (material or non-material) objects, and can therefore be represented as points in conceptual spaces."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ad3ffce2-eb40-4820-86cc-5288755051f5",
